{"type":"message","id":"a7381c59","parentId":"f0bd1e12","timestamp":"2026-05-19T00:32:19.890Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" or similar. But maybe it's an issue with the request. Let me try without the content escaping issues.\n\nActually, the platform returned error 1101 which is a specific error from Cloudflare Workers. Let me try with a different request format - maybe JSON is malformed in some way.\n\nActually wait, I need to double-check: error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers is \"Worker exceeded memory\". But maybe there's something else - let me look at what curl is sending more carefully.\n\nLet me also check if the issue is with the POST body, perhaps there's a size limit or the body isn't being parsed correctly.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-280e262f-5960-44ea-a407-ac0933add2fa","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 00:30 UTC test\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":132,"output":251,"cacheRead":19344,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19727,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779150734606,"responseId":"chatcmpl-18b3303d-7ada-4c69-bb07-6304aaa1ccaf"}}
