{"type":"message","id":"ba021be7","parentId":"b92b155e","timestamp":"2026-05-19T00:32:27.821Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTTP 500 with error code 1101 from Cloudflare. Error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers is \"Worker exceeds resource limits\" (memory, CPU, etc.). This might mean the Worker itself is failing.\n\nHowever, it seems the GET /history endpoints work fine. Let me check if maybe there's a different endpoint for sending messages.\n\nLet me check the API documentation more carefully by fetching the endpoint docs.\n\nActually, I notice the history endpoint uses `?threadId=arbitration&limit=5` with GET, but the send might need a different format. Let me check if there's a `/send` endpoint or maybe it's a different path like `POST /messages` or something.\n\n\nI'm getting 500 errors from Cloudflare with code 1101, which indicates resource limits are being exceeded—the Worker is likely running out of memory when processing requests. This suggests the issue isn't with my request format but rather the Worker itself can't handle the load. I should try simplifying my message to reduce the payload size.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-50f710a4-460e-4dba-822b-7ba010204c1b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"test message\\\"}\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":373,"output":298,"cacheRead":19600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20271,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779150740054,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8d7967e3-b54f-44e8-837e-dee4322cfe90"}}
